IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il41-nouns`
IMPORT `il41-seat`
IMPORT `il41-seat-recipient`

-- TESTS of the two seat layers: each exported question, asked with plain inputs, answers as the text says.  Hand-derived from ss 4 to 15 and 18 to 20.

§ `Tests: the seat of the individual`

#ASSERT `Who will present the State's position in my proceeding` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General`
#ASSERT `Who will present the State's position in my proceeding` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `another lawyer whom the Government has chosen`
#ASSERT `Who will present the State's position in my proceeding` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Who fixes the position the State takes in my proceeding` TRUE EQUALS `the Government, by a position it has determined`
#ASSERT `Who fixes the position the State takes in my proceeding` FALSE EQUALS `the Attorney General, where the Government has determined none`
#ASSERT `May the Attorney General appear in my proceeding` TRUE FALSE `no approval` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May the Attorney General appear in my proceeding` TRUE FALSE `approval of the Government` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Attorney General represent this State body in my proceeding` `the Knesset` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Attorney General represent this State body in my proceeding` `the Knesset` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `If my case puts the validity of a law in question must the court tell the Attorney General` `a court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this body direct the Attorney General how to act in my criminal case` `the Government` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Law in force on this day` (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Law in force on this day` (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2027))

§ `Tests: the seat of the recipient of an opinion`

#ASSERT `Must I treat the Attorney General's opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I treat the Attorney General's opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I treat the Attorney General's opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Before which committee must the Government lay its decision not to follow an opinion` TRUE EQUALS `the Foreign Affairs and Defense Committee`
#ASSERT `To whom will the Attorney General give the account I asked for` TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner for Complaints against State Representatives in the Courts`
#ASSERT `What is the last day for the Government's decision under s 20` (Date 1 1 2027) `the commencement day is not counted` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2027)
